:Namespace Store
⍝ Migration step 5: a data-access layer.
⍝
⍝ The rest of an application calls Store.Customers, Store.Orders, … and never
⍝ ⎕FREAD/⎕FAPPEND directly. Today these functions read component files.
⍝ To move to SQL, rewrite only the bodies below (e.g. with SQAPL, like
⍝ integrations/mysql/apl): every caller keeps working unchanged.
⍝
⍝   Store.Open '/app/sample-scripts/component-files/data'
⍝   c←Store.Customers          ⍝ namespaces: id name city credit_limit joined
⍝   (Store.Customer 3).name
⍝   o←Store.OrdersFor 8
⍝   Store.AddOrder order       ⍝ appends safely (holds the file while writing)
⍝
⍝ Callers get namespaces, not storage details: they don't know or care that a
⍝ customer is component n of customers.dcf.

    ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1
    Folder←''

    ∇ Open folder
    ⍝ Where the data files are
      Folder←folder,('/'≠⊃⌽folder)/'/'
    ∇

    ∇ r←Customers;t;fields;recs
    ⍝ Every customer, as a namespace per customer
      t←Tie'customers'
      fields←⎕FREAD t 2
      recs←⎕FREAD¨t,¨2+⍳¯3+2⊃⎕FSIZE t
      {}⎕FUNTIE t
      r←fields∘Record¨recs
    ∇

    ∇ c←Customer id;all
    ⍝ One customer by id (DOMAIN ERROR if there's no such customer)
      all←Customers
      :If ~(⊂id)∊all.id
          ⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' 11)('Message'('No customer ',⍕id))
      :EndIf
      c←⊃all/⍨all.id=id
    ∇

    ∇ r←Orders;t
    ⍝ Every order (each was stored as a namespace)
      t←Tie'orders'
      r←⎕FREAD¨t,¨⍳¯1+2⊃⎕FSIZE t
      {}⎕FUNTIE t
    ∇

    ∇ r←OrdersFor customer;all
    ⍝ The orders of one customer
      all←Orders
      r←all/⍨all.customer=customer
    ∇

    ∇ n←AddOrder order;t
    ⍝ Append an order. ⎕FHOLD stops two writers from clashing; in SQL this
    ⍝ becomes a transaction. Returns the new component number.
      t←Tie'orders'
      ⎕FHOLD t
      n←order ⎕FAPPEND t
      ⎕FHOLD ⍬
      {}⎕FUNTIE t
    ∇

    Tie←{(Folder,⍵)⎕FTIE 0}
    Record←{n←⎕NS'' ⋄ _←⍺{n⍎⍺,'←⍵'}¨⍵ ⋄ n}     ⍝ field names, values → namespace
:EndNamespace
